# Commits

One topic per commit. Do not mix unrelated features, fixes, chores, CI, tests, and docs.

Subjects must pass `commitlint` (`@commitlint/config-conventional`) so [semantic-release](https://semantic-release.gitbook.io/semantic-release/) can version from `master`/`main`.

```
<type>: <imperative summary>

Optional body: why, not what. Wrap at 100 characters.
```

Types: `feat` (minor), `fix` (patch), `docs`, `ci`, `test`, `chore`. Breaking changes use a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer (major).

```
# ❌ BAD — one commit, many topics
feat: add JUnit, fix tag-hook tests, and update the README

# ✅ GOOD — split
test: write JUnit XML for nix-unit, BATS, and nixosTest
fix: unset CI variables in tag-hook tests that simulate a local git tag
docs: document JUnit reports, act, and Nix store caching
```

If a file spans topics, stage only the hunks that belong in that commit. Commit only when asked.
